Property: A box not placed from the page's own text, on a page that is not plain and that no ink plan covers, writes the page as an image.
Area: page mode (Detection)
Test command: DEVELOPER_DIR=/Applications/Xcode-27.2.app/Contents/Developer xcodebuild test -scheme ResectaApp -destination id=<simulator> -only-testing:ResectaAppTests/ScannedPageBoxFloorTests
Must go red: ResectaAppTests/ScannedPageBoxFloorTests "a hand-drawn box on a page with a picture writes the page as an image"; ResectaAppTests/ScannedPageBoxFloorTests "a hand-drawn box on a page with a Type 3 font writes the page as an image"; ResectaAppTests/ScannedPageBoxFloorTests "a hand-drawn box on a page with an inline picture writes the page as an image"; ResectaAppTests/ScannedPageBoxFloorTests "a duplicated box on a page with a picture writes the page as an image"; ResectaAppTests/ScannedPageBoxFloorTests "a match moved by hand on a page with a picture writes the page as an image"; ResectaAppTests/ScannedPageBoxFloorTests "matches moved together by hand on a page with a picture write the page as an image"; ResectaAppTests/ScannedPageBoxFloorTests "a match read from the page's picture on a page with a picture writes the page as an image"; ResectaAppTests/ScannedPageBoxFloorTests "one hand-drawn box beside a placed match on a page with a picture writes the page as an image"
Note: a page that shows text in an invisible render mode (the scanned page, the invisible-text page) is written as an image for that reason before this rule is read, so its cases do not go red here; the invisible-text faults (page-mode-invisible-text-*) cover them.
Apply in a scratch worktree with `git apply`; discard after.

